#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Log saved Cronometer foods from the terminal.

Cronometer has no public API for personal accounts. Its web app talks to the
server over GWT-RPC, so this tool logs in the way the website does and replays
the "add food" request the web app sent when the food was first added by hand.
Replaying the browser's own request keeps the serving size, unit, and diary
group exactly as the website records them, without decoding every field.

The login flow, build hash lookup, and the authenticate and removeServing
payloads follow github.com/cphoskins/cronometer-mcp (MIT license).
"""

